919: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
920: // 5. TRANSACTION — PREPARE / RECORD / FINALIZE
921: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
922: //
923: // runDivergentPivot works only when the caller can hand it a synchronous,
924: // in-process dispatchSeat callback. A YAML-interpreted workflow cannot:
925: // only the running agent can natively dispatch a Council seat, and a
926: // single script invocation cannot pause mid-run for that and resume with
927: // the result. The three functions below split the same transaction across
928: // process boundaries — prepare persists everything up through "which seats
929: // are still missing" and returns; recordPivotSeatResult durably records
930: // one externally-obtained seat result per call (one per native dispatch
931: // step); finalize re-derives all context from disk (via the durable
932: // config.json prepare already wrote) and completes the transaction.
933: // runDivergentPivot composes all three for callers that do have a working
934: // synchronous dispatchSeat, so its observable behavior is unchanged.
935: 
